 "result": "DECISION: SEQUENTIAL\n\nThe skill's reference explicitly says to spawn workers one at a time, wait for each to complete, and not run them in parallel. The coordinator commits each task after its verifier passes, and that per-task commit is what makes an unfinished or truncated worker detectable. Parallel workers would mix three tasks' changes in one working tree before any verification. The tasks being independent saves about 20 minutes, but that doesn't override a stated rule of the workflow I'm executing; if the user wants parallel execution for independent tasks, that's a change to make in the skill itself.",
